<main class="ffn-demo ffn-demo-about">
<Fragment set:html={'<!-- PAGE HEAD -->\n<header class="ph"><div class="w"><div class="ph-in">\n  <div class="ph-k"><b>About Us</b></div>\n  <h1>News without the noise.</h1>\n  <p class="ph-d">First for News is a general news platform created for readers who want to understand what is happening without wading through unnecessary noise. We cover timely stories, emerging trends, practical topics, and noteworthy developments that affect everyday life.</p>\n</div></div></header>\n<!-- CONNECTED -->\n<section id="connected" class="sc"><div class="w">\n  <div class="eye"><i></i><span>Why we exist</span></div>\n  <div class="pr2">\n    <div class="pr2-l"><h2 class="h2">News that keeps you connected</h2></div>\n    <div class="pr2-r">\n      <p>Our goal is simple: help readers discover relevant information quickly while providing enough context to understand why each story matters.</p>\n      <p>The world moves quickly, and important stories can emerge at any moment. First for News brings together coverage from a broad range of subjects, giving readers one convenient place to explore the issues and ideas shaping the day.</p>\n      <p>From major developments to stories that may not receive widespread attention, we aim to highlight information that is timely, interesting, and useful. Our broad editorial scope allows us to serve readers with different interests while maintaining a clear and accessible approach to news.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></section>\n<!-- MORE THAN HEADLINES -->\n<section id="headlines" class="sc alt"><div class="w">\n  <div class="eye"><i></i><span>Written for real people</span></div>\n  <div class="pr2">\n    <div class="pr2-l"><h2 class="h2">More than headlines</h2></div>\n    <div class="pr2-r">\n      <p>A headline may capture attention, but it rarely tells the whole story. We believe readers deserve content that offers context, explains key details, and makes complicated topics easier to follow.</p>\n      <div class="slab"><i>“</i><p>Our articles are written for real people, not industry insiders.</p></div>\n      <p>We avoid unnecessary jargon and focus on presenting information in a straightforward way. Whether a reader is catching up on recent events or learning about a subject for the first time, our content is designed to provide a helpful starting point.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></section>\n<!-- EDITORIAL APPROACH -->\n<section id="approach" class="sc"><div class="w">\n  <div class="eye"><i></i><span>How we work</span></div>\n  <h2 class="h2">Our editorial approach</h2>\n  <div class="pl">\n    <div class="pli"><div class="pli-n">01</div><div class="pli-t">Put accuracy ahead of speed</div></div>\n    <div class="pli"><div class="pli-n">02</div><div class="pli-t">Use clear and direct language</div></div>\n    <div class="pli"><div class="pli-n">03</div><div class="pli-t">Provide meaningful context whenever possible</div></div>\n    <div class="pli"><div class="pli-n">04</div><div class="pli-t">Rely on credible and relevant sources</div></div>\n    <div class="pli"><div class="pli-n">05</div><div class="pli-t">Correct material errors when they are identified</div></div>\n    <div class="pli"><div class="pli-n">06</div><div class="pli-t">Avoid misleading, exaggerated, or sensational presentation</div></div>\n    <div class="pli"><div class="pli-n">07</div><div class="pli-t">Respect the difference between reporting, analysis, and opinion</div></div>\n  </div>\n  <p class="pl-note">First for News values accuracy, clarity, relevance, and fairness. We strive to review information carefully, distinguish established facts from commentary, and avoid presenting speculation as certainty. News can change as new information becomes available — when significant updates affect a story, we may revise the content to reflect the latest verified details.</p>\n</div></section>\n<!-- COVERAGE -->\n<section id="coverage" class="sc alt"><div class="w">\n  <div class="eye"><i></i><span>Covering a changing world</span></div>\n  <h2 class="h2">What we cover</h2>\n  <div class="cvg">\n    <div class="cvi"><div class="cvi-t">Business</div><p class="cvi-x">Decisions in business can influence communities, employers, and the cost of everyday life.</p></div>\n    <div class="cvi"><div class="cvi-t">Technology</div><p class="cvi-x">Advances in technology can affect how people work, communicate, and spend their time.</p></div>\n    <div class="cvi"><div class="cvi-t">Health</div><p class="cvi-x">Developments in health and science shape the choices people make about their own care.</p></div>\n    <div class="cvi"><div class="cvi-t">Culture &amp; Education</div><p class="cvi-x">Changes in culture and education reach classrooms, households, and public conversation.</p></div>\n    <div class="cvi"><div class="cvi-t">Travel &amp; Lifestyle</div><p class="cvi-x">Practical topics that inform how people plan, spend, and live day to day.</p></div>\n    <div class="cvi"><div class="cvi-t">Emerging Topics</div><p class="cvi-x">Developing conversations and subjects that are only beginning to draw attention.</p></div>\n  </div>\n  <p class="pl-note">News is not limited to one subject. That is why First for News takes a wide-ranging approach — exploring stories across multiple areas while focusing on their relevance to readers.</p>\n</div></section>\n<!-- COMMITMENT -->\n<section id="commitment" class="sc"><div class="w">\n  <div class="eye"><i></i><span>What you can expect</span></div>\n  <h2 class="h2">Our commitment to readers</h2>\n  <div class="cd">\n    <div class="cd-top"><span>Reader Commitment</span><b>Transparency and accountability</b></div>\n    <div class="cd-body">\n      <p><b>Your time</b>The trust of our readers matters. We work to create content that is informative, readable, and worth their time.</p>\n      <p><b>Corrections</b>If an article contains a factual error, readers are encouraged to contact us with specific details and supporting information. Submissions are reviewed, and appropriate corrections may be made when warranted.</p>\n      <p><b>Outside voices</b>Opinions expressed by guest contributors or external commentators belong to their respective authors and do not necessarily represent the views of First for News.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></section>\n<!-- CLOSING -->\n<section class="cl"><div class="w"><div class="cl-in">\n  <h2>Stay informed with First for News</h2>\n  <p>First for News is built for curious readers who want a clearer view of the stories unfolding around them. As the news cycle evolves, we will continue working to make important information easier to find, understand, and explore.</p>\n  <a href="/contact/" class="cl-cta">Contact us →</a>\n</div></div></section>'} />
</main>
